55,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Candidate A is a catalogue, which Daisuke noted is durable, but it relies on field sites, which Takumi warned against.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Candidate B uses simulation, which is free! But it also uses spectroscopy... and Takumi said that's broken!","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,Candidate C uses breeding colonies... the portfolio review said those overran their schedules twice as often.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Takumi,,A is out because of the field sites. B is out because the spectroscopy suite is a disaster.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Candidate D requires glasshouses, but I found they are booked solid for two more cycles. It cannot start.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Servas,,"If D is blocked by space and C by schedule risks, we must look closer at A and B.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Sakura,,But A needs to ship samples! I saw that shipping costs are climbing while other things are frozen!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,A is a catalogue project. Those are the ones that kept earning their keep for a decade.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Takumi,,I can't support A if the field sites are burning or flooding. That's exactly the kind of interruption I hate.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Minako,,"If the animal facility is the only thing with spare, accredited capacity, Candidate C is the most viable infrastructure-wise.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Minako, but the risk of schedule overrun for breeding colonies is high. Is the stability of the facility worth that?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"What about B? If they do more simulation and less spectroscopy, it's super cheap and the staff are available!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think A is the safest for the scientific community, even if the field work is hard.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Takumi,,No way. A and B both rely on things that are currently failing. C is the only one where the facility is actually ready.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Minako,,I agree. The animal facility is accredited and has vet cover. It is the only reliable foundation here.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Servas,,"I see the logic. While C has schedule risks, the other three face immediate infrastructure or staffing walls.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Sakura,,I guess C is the winner then! I hope the salamanders are cute!,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,If everyone agrees... I will go with the one that has the best facility support.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"Finally, a choice that doesn't rely on a broken machine or a flooded forest.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Minako,,It is the most pragmatic choice given the current constraints.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
